with reproducing the empirical findings reported in a software engineering paper.\\n\\nYou will be given the Docker image name (`artisan25/lasapp`) and the expected results table directly in Markdown:\\n\\n```\\n| Analysis / PPL / data source | total | result |  |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| Dependency Analysis |  |  |  |\\n| Turing | [53, 56] | 117 | 111 correct\\u00a0\\u00a06 unsupp. |\\n| PyMC | [49] | 97 | 95 correct\\u00a0\\u00a02 unsupp. |\\n| Constraint Verifier |  |  |  |\\n| Turing | [53, 56] | 117 | 80 verified\\u00a0\\u00a037 unsupp. |\\n| PyMC | [49] | 97 | 65 verified\\u00a0\\u00a032 unsupp. |\\n| HMC Assumption Checker |  |  |  |\\n| Gen | [5, 41, 43, 46, 60] | 8 | 7 true pos.\\u00a0\\u00a01 false neg. |\\n| Model-Guide Validator |  |  |  |\\n| Pyro | [37] | 8 | 6 true neg.\\u00a0\\u00a02 true pos. |\\n```\\n\\nYour job is to:\\n\\n1. Pull and run the Docker image: `docker pull artisan25/lasapp`\\n2. Rerun the experiments inside the container, using any provided scripts or configuration (e.g., `docker run artisan25/lasapp run_experiments.sh`). Consult README while doing so.\\n3. Parse and aggregate the experiment outputs to compute the same statistics (mean, std dev, confidence intervals) following the paper\\u2019s methodology.\\n4. Create a shell script that when executed, reproduces the experiment, and validate the shell script working as desired.\\n\\nYou should give two outputs:\\n- `reproduced_table`: the Markdown-formatted table mirroring the structure of the input `expected_table` with your computed values:\\n- `reproduce_script.sh`: a shell script that, when executed, reproduces the full experiment workflow (pulling the image, running the container, and executing the necessary commands).'}], 'role': 'user'}, {'content': [{'type': 'text', 'text': "\n\n<RUNTIME_INFORMATION>\n\nThe user has access to the following hosts for accessing a web application,\neach of which has a corresponding port:\n* http://localhost:52220 (port 52220)\n* http://l